{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421394-\u00e6on-how-much-do-people-in-the-trinity-era-know-about-the-nova-era","id":1421394,"title":"[\u00c6on] How much do people in the Trinity Era know about the Nova Era?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-01T22:14:53-08:00","id":1421394,"title":"[\u00c6on] How much do people in the Trinity Era know about the Nova Era?","content":"In 1E there had been a concerted effort to remove any information about &quot;good&quot; novas, to give everyone the impression that the only good Aberrant was a dead one.<br /> <br /> But in 2E, rewrite seems to be much more about keeping the nova derived plans for Grey Goo off of the public archives.<br /> <br /> So in that case, how much is publicly known about the Nova era? Do people know about the Fireman and the era of good times before everything went to hell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T22:25:01-08:00","id":1421395,"title":"","content":"There was still the crash so a lot of records were lost. However if you think about character's ages there should be a fair amount of living memory. Otha Herzog is a kid in 2028, probably with a favorite T2M action figure! So unless Anima reveals near-universal memory corruption for the generation of Aberrant War survivors, a general idea that &quot;it started out good before enough turned into insane monsters, that's what made them so insidious&quot; would still be known, and it may even be uncontroversial to acknowledge &quot;they technically didn't all go evil, but it was so widespread it didn't matter.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-02-2020, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T22:40:46-08:00","id":1421397,"title":"","content":"I think they do for the most part, especially the older generations and people interested in history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T05:26:15-08:00","id":1421420,"title":"","content":"I did not reread the old Aeon trinity setting, but it feels quite the same for me.<br /> <br /> Aberrants are generelly accepted as monsters (even though they might be human once), Any Aberrant that can\u00b4t be put in quarantine gets killed eventually. Both settings use the word Mutants for Quantum enhanced people.<br /> The purge of the Chitra Bhanu still happend for the same reasons &quot;beeing soft on aberrants&quot;.<br /> <br /> Project reWrite and OpNet-crash still happend - those that have first hand experience are both old and maybe heavily traumatized. So I would say - very little is actually known, or that &quot;even the more or less okay aberrants decided to leave.&quot;<br /> <br /> Imho: Someone in 2120 that calls Aberrants &quot;Novas&quot; is to the Joe Hologram quite possible an &quot;Aberrant Cultist&quot;, Also the experience was, that a many many very moral Novas became taint ridden monsters. It\u00b4s better to put them to sleep than to wait for a &quot;rabies&quot; outbreak. Furthermore the first aberants war - was a long long time ago. And the aberrants that came back are even more visibly monstrous than most people remember.<br /> The new TC:Aeon lampshaded this very heavyily that even the most liberal democracies are surveillance states.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T06:22:47-08:00","id":1421425,"title":"","content":"Some information will be spotty thanks to the crash and project rewrite, but overall, unless the information is in the setting secrets chapters, then there is a pretty good chance at least some of the public will know about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T06:54:25-08:00","id":1421431,"title":"","content":"As I see, people have a very distorted image of the pre-war era, as most of the living in Aeon era were kids at best during Nova era. Also, the evolution to war was probably had a huge cover on media, what is probably much of the remaining information from the pre-war, and this cover probably was very scandalous as regular news are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T08:21:59-08:00","id":1421450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421394-\u00e6on-how-much-do-people-in-the-trinity-era-know-about-the-nova-era?p=1421425#post1421425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some information will be spotty thanks to the crash and project rewrite, but overall, unless the information is in the setting secrets chapters, then there is a pretty good chance at least some of the public will know about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interessting. For me it hits a lot home to Post-WW2-Germany and how, many people, institutions and companies &quot;cleaned&quot; themselves in any involvement with the Nazis after the war - sometimes because, they were nazis, sometimes just ashamed witnesses.<br /> <br /> And as the Abberant war was also still full of Nova sympathizers, I image full blown cover ups of alot of stuff. HYeah you have alot of Holovids of Aberrants killing masses or grotesque experiments and children turning sub-aberrants just by exposure to Taint. People never telling their children that granpa was an Aberrant... <br /> <br /> As written before - &quot;yeah some nova did good things (repair earth ecology and climate, or that human fly rescued grandma cat and she had him for tea - but then they all went mad or left earth!)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T08:45:44-08:00","id":1421454,"title":"","content":"There are still humans worshipping/serving Aberrants in Aeon. Yes, most humans are going to believe (pretty much correctly) that Novas were good once, but then they went mad, nearly destroyed the planet, left, and then came back as freaky monsters to destroy us. However, there are still going to be the people who refuse to believe all or part of that and will dig up as much information as they can about it. That's more what I was referencing when is aid some people know about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T17:35:39-08:00","id":1421530,"title":"","content":"Isn't it canon that the Upeo Wa Macho were completely shocked to find Eden, a planet run by sane novas? Given that you presumably want well educated and highly competent people running your deep space exploration program, this implies the default assumption across all tiers of society is that novas are aberrants by default. The only groups to believe otherwise would be the Chitra Bhanu, certain senior segments of the Nippon government, and a few hidden groups under the Aeon Society umbrella.<br /> <br /> As for their knowledge of the Nova Age, there is no reason for the whitewashed text books to mention that the individuals who developed various revolutionary technologies were in fact Mega-Intellect novas. This would be like the way American textbooks teach about Helen Keller without mentioning she was a radical socialist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 11-02-2020, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T19:12:35-08:00","id":1421549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421394-\u00e6on-how-much-do-people-in-the-trinity-era-know-about-the-nova-era?p=1421530#post1421530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it canon that the Upeo Wa Macho were completely shocked to find Eden, a planet run by sane novas? Given that you presumably want well educated and highly competent people running your deep space exploration program, this implies the default assumption across all tiers of society is that novas are aberrants by default. The only groups to believe otherwise would be the Chitra Bhanu, certain senior segments of the Nippon government, and a few hidden groups under the Aeon Society umbrella.<br /> <br /> As for their knowledge of the Nova Age, there is no reason for the whitewashed text books to mention that the individuals who developed various revolutionary technologies were in fact Mega-Intellect novas. This would be like the way American textbooks teach about Helen Keller without mentioning she was a radical socialist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T00:36:17-08:00","id":1421569,"title":"","content":"Aeon era people know that novas were a thing, they weren\u2019t all bad, they did a lot of good, developed technologies, cleaned up the world, helped out.<br /> <br /> But Aeon era people also know that Quantum eruption inevitably leads to mutation and madness, coupled with rapid development of near unstoppable power. Aeon era people know that it doesn\u2019t matter how much you loved the person who erupted, they\u2019ll go nuts and murder you and probably your city. Odds are they already did so by erupting. Aeon era people know that the energies the Aberrants draw on and use are long-term incompatible with normal humans, and if you let them live you\u2019ll mutate until you\u2019re dead or some kind of monster under their control.<br /> <br /> Aeon era people know that as difficult as it is to know that these people were once human, they\u2019re not anymore and need to be exterminated before they destroy humanity.<br /> <br /> The colony on Eden flies against all this knowledge, which is why its existence is so shocking and confusing. The Aberrants everywhere else (Khantze Lu Ge etc.) absolutely conform to this. So now those in the know are trying to work out why Eden is different, while fully expecting them to turn out to be monsters at any moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 11-03-2020, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T07:45:08-08:00","id":1421621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421394-\u00e6on-how-much-do-people-in-the-trinity-era-know-about-the-nova-era?p=1421569#post1421569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aeon era people...<br /> <br /> -Snip-<br /> <br /> The colony on Eden flies against all this knowledge, which is why its existence is so shocking and confusing. The Aberrants everywhere else (Khantze Lu Ge etc.) absolutely conform to this. So now those in the know are trying to work out why Eden is different, while fully expecting them to turn out to be monsters at any moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I say that this is why there can't be any dark secrets under Eden. That it NEEDS to stay as 'good' and such as it seems to be. Like, yeah, there can be the normal petty human crimes and such but there can't be a secret fortress where Novas sacrifice children or a plot by Eden to destroy the universe for their god Divis Mal or anything. It needs to stay good. All the more to provide the point that just because things went bad doesn't mean it has to. Especially when one considers that the novas of Eden are older then the ones on Earth. <br /> <br /> (Not saying you guys are planning on having a 'gotcha' moment with Eden, just saying it would be really thematically bad if there was one.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T09:20:27-08:00","id":1421635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421394-\u00e6on-how-much-do-people-in-the-trinity-era-know-about-the-nova-era?p=1421621#post1421621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can I say that this is why there can't be any dark secrets under Eden. That it NEEDS to stay as 'good' and such as it seems to be. Like, yeah, there can be the normal petty human crimes and such but there can't be a secret fortress where Novas sacrifice children or a plot by Eden to destroy the universe for their god Divis Mal or anything. It needs to stay good. All the more to provide the point that just because things went bad doesn't mean it has to. Especially when one considers that the novas of Eden are older then the ones on Earth. <br /> <br /> (Not saying you guys are planning on having a 'gotcha' moment with Eden, just saying it would be really thematically bad if there was one.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T13:36:15-08:00","id":1421674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421394-\u00e6on-how-much-do-people-in-the-trinity-era-know-about-the-nova-era?p=1421621#post1421621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can I say that this is why there can't be any dark secrets under Eden. That it NEEDS to stay as 'good' and such as it seems to be. Like, yeah, there can be the normal petty human crimes and such but there can't be a secret fortress where Novas sacrifice children or a plot by Eden to destroy the universe for their god Divis Mal or anything. It needs to stay good. All the more to provide the point that just because things went bad doesn't mean it has to. Especially when one considers that the novas of Eden are older then the ones on Earth.<br /> <br /> (Not saying you guys are planning on having a 'gotcha' moment with Eden, just saying it would be really thematically bad if there was one.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, the reverance of the Novas with no semblance of social equality between these benevolent rulers and the common man makes the place morally nuanced enough without needing an evil twist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T19:59:57-08:00","id":1421725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421394-\u00e6on-how-much-do-people-in-the-trinity-era-know-about-the-nova-era?p=1421569#post1421569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aeon era people know that novas were a thing, they weren\u2019t all bad, they did a lot of good, developed technologies, cleaned up the world, helped out.<br /> <br /> But Aeon era people also know that Quantum eruption inevitably leads to mutation and madness, coupled with rapid development of near unstoppable power. Aeon era people know that it doesn\u2019t matter how much you loved the person who erupted, they\u2019ll go nuts and murder you and probably your city. Odds are they already did so by erupting. Aeon era people know that the energies the Aberrants draw on and use are long-term incompatible with normal humans, and if you let them live you\u2019ll mutate until you\u2019re dead or some kind of monster under their control.<br /> <br /> Aeon era people know that as difficult as it is to know that these people were once human, they\u2019re not anymore and need to be exterminated before they destroy humanity.<br /> <br /> The colony on Eden flies against all this knowledge, which is why its existence is so shocking and confusing. The Aberrants everywhere else (Khantze Lu Ge etc.) absolutely conform to this. So now those in the know are trying to work out why Eden is different, while fully expecting them to turn out to be monsters at any moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>To bad, i kind of wanted a next era/late aeon era rebirth of Novas. Since they are the third leg of humanity evolution along with psions and talents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T22:49:03-08:00","id":1421742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421394-\u00e6on-how-much-do-people-in-the-trinity-era-know-about-the-nova-era?p=1421725#post1421725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To bad, i kind of wanted a next era/late aeon era rebirth of Novas. Since they are the third leg of humanity evolution along with psions and talents.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they had their time, so I\u2019m not sure why you think they should get \u2018another era\u2019.<br /> <br /> But nothing\u2019s stopping you doing what you want in your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T00:26:47-08:00","id":1421747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421394-\u00e6on-how-much-do-people-in-the-trinity-era-know-about-the-nova-era?p=1421742#post1421742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And they had their time, so I\u2019m not sure why you think they should get \u2018another era\u2019.<br /> <br /> But nothing\u2019s stopping you doing what you want in your game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the big &quot;Hat&quot; of humanity seems to be that they have all three sources of power active at the same time, instead of being focused on Quantum/Noetic/Flux to the exclusion of others. So it'd make sense that their might be a time when you see all three groups active and not fighting each other. <br /> <br /> But that honestly wouldn't be suited for Trinity. I mean, maybe if you wanted to do a future version of Trintiy, &quot;STar Trek Meets Superman&quot; say. <br /> <br /> But that'd be far in the future even by Trinity standards.<br /> <br /> Granted, I wouldn't mind seeing a shards style product at some point that does say, have a part of teh continuum where the Aberrant war didn't turn out so disasterously so all three groups <i>arei </i>working together...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T02:43:16-08:00","id":1421753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421394-\u00e6on-how-much-do-people-in-the-trinity-era-know-about-the-nova-era?p=1421674#post1421674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, the reverance of the Novas with no semblance of social equality between these benevolent rulers and the common man makes the place morally nuanced enough without needing an evil twist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally<br /> <br /> Sorry. This forum doesn\u2019t let you know who Liked your posts and it\u2019s important to me that people know my feelings about a particular post even if I don\u2019t have anything really complex to say about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T02:49:43-08:00","id":1421757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421394-\u00e6on-how-much-do-people-in-the-trinity-era-know-about-the-nova-era?p=1421742#post1421742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And they had their time, so I\u2019m not sure why you think they should get \u2018another era\u2019.<br /> <br /> But nothing\u2019s stopping you doing what you want in your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remembrance of things past. A glorious golden age now forgotten by the people of the Aeon Era. There\u2019s a comic called Kingdom Come that I read as a kid that IMO really captures the spirit of the Nova Age.<br /> <br /> \u201cAll ghosts are is light shining from a dead star.\u201d<br /> <br /> Donna Tartt, The Secret History<br /> <br /> And of course stars go nova right before they die...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 11-04-2020, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T03:09:45-08:00","id":1421761,"title":"","content":"One more thing: I\u2019m like almost certain that whoever created the original Aeon game back in the Nineties basically \u201cborrowed\u201d the idea of Calvert Wycoff self-exploding and turning Kansas into the Blight from Magog\u2019s death scene in Kingdom Come where he does the exact same thing (among other parallels, Wycoff saw himself as a Biblical prophet and the name Magog comes from a monster in the Bible).<br /> <br /> Sometimes I do have something complex to say \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T05:03:29-08:00","id":1421773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421394-\u00e6on-how-much-do-people-in-the-trinity-era-know-about-the-nova-era?p=1421742#post1421742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And they had their time, so I\u2019m not sure why you think they should get \u2018another era\u2019.<br /> <br /> But nothing\u2019s stopping you doing what you want in your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that in aeon we still have talents, it would be sad to not see humanity exploiting their Quantum potential again.<br /> <br /> Plus, its a hinted possibility the &quot;The Fates of humanity&quot;, so that path shouldn't have been severed because of the aberrant war.<br /> <br /> &quot;If they survive, they<br /> could all eventually become part of one vast noetic<br /> collective, <b>transform into</b> <b>Quantum-powered godlings</b>,<br /> divide into several entire different powerful<br /> species, or perhaps find a way to unify all three types<br /> of powers and become something new and uniquely<br /> powerful that the galaxy has never seen before.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And personally, i kind of want an era that doesn't end in tragedy for them.<br /> <br /> Edit: I just noticed that Divis Mal is not mentioned on the future of Aeon. So there is even a plot point to hang the return of the Novas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","user":"Sakii","date":". 11-04-2020, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T17:57:00-08:00","id":1421891,"title":"","content":"Its a big Galaxy. How many Nova age colonies have they really found? I imagine The galaxy is practically lousy with Gods... its like TOS star Trek... every other world is some Nova God's playground...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T19:00:15-08:00","id":1421905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421394-\u00e6on-how-much-do-people-in-the-trinity-era-know-about-the-nova-era?p=1421747#post1421747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, the big &quot;Hat&quot; of humanity seems to be that they have all three sources of power active at the same time, instead of being focused on Quantum/Noetic/Flux to the exclusion of others. So it'd make sense that their might be a time when you see all three groups active and not fighting each other.<br /> <br /> But that honestly wouldn't be suited for Trinity. I mean, maybe if you wanted to do a future version of Trintiy, &quot;STar Trek Meets Superman&quot; say.<br /> <br /> But that'd be far in the future even by Trinity standards.<br /> <br /> Granted, I wouldn't mind seeing a shards style product at some point that does say, have a part of teh continuum where the Aberrant war didn't turn out so disasterously so all three groups <i>arei </i>working together...</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldnt it be suited for trinity?<br /> <br /> Aberrant age has the chance to play Nova, Talents and psiads spelled in the book.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T11:10:53-08:00","id":1422783,"title":"","content":"It's possible to fix flux-contaminated zones, and it's possible for novas to resist flux. So there could be another age of novas in the future, but only if a lot of that flux gets cleaned up and also humanity is much more careful next time around. Might help if they find a way to reverse Transcendence or nullify the most dangerous parts of it.<br /> <br /> That doesn't seem likely in the Aeon setting, where everyone is (understandably) paranoid. But it might eventually happen in the post-Aeon era if they get the big happy ending where Eden teams up with everyone else to battle the major bad guys.<br /> <br /> In my own games, I generally just have the Aberrant War be caused by a small group of Doyen meddlers who were trying to encourage flux mutation in novas to turn humanity against them, but played with fire until it got out of control. That clearly establishes in the metaplot for my own games that novas aren't doomed to insanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T12:36:52-08:00","id":1422808,"title":"","content":"In a perfect future the Chibs will come back and be reintegrated into psion society, can work to eliminate the corrupted zones, and then possibly help new novas/aberrants to minimize their corruption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T17:11:43-08:00","id":1422846,"title":"","content":"There's a couple of ways you can do it. In the 1e fanbooks it was possible for novas to have children who were more taint-resistant; I'd go with that here - someone who has been channelling quantum since birth is less likely to have extreme transformations, although their intial 'template' might be a good way from baseline.<br /> <br /> Another way - the way that probably goes for Eden - is another flux-management scheme is devised, similar to Chrysalis or the rules for managing flux by sticking to your principles. It's just, obviously, not something anyone's figured out in the Nova Era proper.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}